    "Calibration pairs are written by hand from the source, before any judge output was seen. Kinds: supported, supported_absence (a correct claim that something is missing), wrong_claim (real path, false statement), invented_behaviour (real symbol, behaviour it does not have).",
    "labels holds verdicts for pairs the recorded pipeline produced. Copy key, claim and citation from the support suite's 'pair/' cases; use supported=null when the text states no fact about the code."
